# New York State Design System

> The New York State Design System (NYSDS) is a shared library of web components, design tokens, styles, and guidance that helps teams across 45+ New York State agencies build accessible, consistent websites and applications. The New York State Office of Information Technology Services (ITS) maintains it.

Key facts:

- Website: {{ site.url }}/
- Code components are framework-agnostic web components (custom elements with an `nys-` prefix, such as `<nys-button>`). They work in plain HTML and in Angular, React, Vue, and .NET applications.
- npm packages: `@nysds/components` (web components) and `@nysds/styles` (CSS, design tokens, agency themes, and utility classes).
- Every component is tested against WCAG 2.2 before release.
- AI coding assistants can query component APIs, design tokens, and usage guidance through the NYSDS MCP server, published on npm as `@nysds/mcp-server`.
- Source code: https://github.com/ITS-HCD/nysds

